

-> ResponseEntity (Status codes & headers)
    ResponseEntity gives full control over response.

    @GetMapping("/{id}")
    public ResponseEntity<UserDTO> getUser(@PathVariable Long id) {
        UserDTO dto = userService.getUserById(id);
        return ResponseEntity
                .status(HttpStatus.OK)
                .body(dto);
    }


->  DTO Pattern (Why not expose Entity)
   ❌ Problem
      Entity contains DB structure
      Security risk
      Tight coupling

        @Entity
        public class User {
            @Id
            private Long id;
            private String name;
            private String password; // ❌ sensitive
        }


-> Path Variables & Query Parameters
   Path Variable

   Used to identify specific resource

   inside postman -> GET /users/10

   @GetMapping("/{id}")
   public UserDTO get(@PathVariable Long id) {
       return userService.getUserById(id);
   }
